  "known_assembly_process_issues": [
    "U7 pads7,9,16,18,19 contain ordinary open plated vias in their solder lands. Factory stencil/reflow may lose solder through these vias. A factory must explicitly accept a qualified prefill/plug/cap process or the layout must be changed; ordinary low-cost assembly is not yet approved.",
    "R4 uses double-sided component placement: D2 on back, other fitted parts on front. A one-sided SMT assembly quote cannot cover all five SMD parts.",
    "RP2040-Zero-M is directly soldered through23pins in current BOM; embedded footprint description says socketed but sockets are not bought. Actual underside component clearance and module/header fit need physical validation.",
    "D1 body needs3–5mm stand-off and rear D2/solder joints needat least5mm insulated support clearance. Actual lead formation/heights and cooling are not validated by2D DRC.",
    "Actual delivered driver revision, socket contact shape/current/height, heatsink interface/adhesive, terminal/jack lead tolerances, fan/cable access and enclosure fit remain receipt/assembly checks."
  ],
